# Rascal settings layered on ArduPilot's plane.parm (--defaults plane.parm,rascal.parm).
# FixedWing6DOF has no stall model (level-flight stall would be near 8.3 m/s),
# so keep ArduPlane well above it.
AIRSPEED_MIN 15
# Elevator and rudder are reversed, as ArduPilot's own JSBSim Rascal frame does
# (models/plane-reverse-servo-pitch-yaw.parm) and C++'s servo_map did (x-1).
# FixedWing6DOF uses the standard sign convention: positive elevator pitches the
# nose down (C_M_delta_elevator < 0) and positive rudder yaws it left
# (C_N_delta_rudder < 0), while ArduPlane's positive outputs mean nose up and
# nose right. Aileron already agrees (C_L_delta_aileron > 0 rolls right).
# Reversed here only: ArduPilotBridge's maps stay plain.
SERVO2_REVERSED 1
SERVO4_REVERSED 1
# Sensor noise: SITL's SIM_ defaults for now. Noise belongs here, not in scrimmage.
